---
# Inherits the root configuration; the entries below are test-only relaxations.
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access

# Why bugprone-unchecked-optional-access is off here, and only here:
#
# GoogleTest's ASSERT_* macros expand to a bare `return` on failure. That is
# real control flow, but clang-tidy's dataflow analysis does not model it, so
#
#     ASSERT_TRUE(maybe.has_value());
#     EXPECT_EQ(*maybe, expected);
#
# is reported as an unchecked access even though the dereference is
# unreachable when the value is absent. Rewriting every such test to satisfy
# the analyzer makes the tests worse, and blanket NOLINT comments scattered
# through the suite hide the cases where the warning would be correct.
#
# The check stays ON for src/, where it is genuinely useful and where there
# are no ASSERT_* macros to confuse it.
